  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from Alaska Medicaid Tremfya (guselkumab), Version 1. Original 10/10/2024; Accepted 11/15/2024; Effective 01/01/2025.",
    "Closed indication labels represent FDA indication severity and systemic therapy or phototherapy candidacy for PsO. All three indications require adults (age \u226518). Phototherapy candidacy does not permit concurrent phototherapy.",
    "Specialty gap: no prescriber specialty requirement is specified in this PDF.",
    "All three indications require trial and failure of a TNF blocker and at least one other therapy; PsO includes at least one topical agent. No minimum trial duration is specified.",
    "Indication-gated activity: PsO PASI \u226512 (or equivalent); PsA HAQ-DI \u22652 (or equivalent); UC baseline Mayo score (or equivalent) submitted, without a numeric threshold.",
    "Initial authorization (notes only): monitoring plan; previous therapies trialed and nature of failure; complete medication regimen; confirmation patient is not receiving concurrent phototherapy; requested dosing conforms to an FDA-approved regimen by indication. Documentation requires manual review.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization approval up to 12 months. No separate reauthorization clinical criteria are specified.",
    "No QUANTITY LIMIT section in this PDF. Dosing per FDA label by indication requires manual review; no numeric quantity or days-supply limits are encoded.",
    "Cautions (notes only): evaluate for tuberculosis (TB) before initiating guselkumab; do not initiate with active TB. No live vaccines during treatment. Serious hypersensitivity reactions including anaphylaxis have been reported. Infection risk: discontinue if a clinically significant infection develops until it resolves.",
    "PDL context: all TREMFYA rows are non_preferred. Preferred cytokine peers without packs include Humira, Hadlima and Rinvoq (notes only). Linked alternatives require indication-specific review and do not imply confirmed coverage.",
    "This pack remains partial: initial documentation, monitoring, duration, reauthorization, FDA dosing and cautions require manual review."
  ],
